{"id":1366,"date":"2020-11-26T20:21:38","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T04:21:38","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1366"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:40","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:40","slug":"program-the-crab-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-crab-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Crab Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404ac4\" name=\"6a22165404ac4\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Briefing videos<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]These videos go over how to program your Crab Bot. Don&#8217;t forget to go through the rest of the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Njkp6r53Vas&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=HJqWuFykMiE&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404beb\" name=\"6a22165404beb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What does it do?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Just like the nocturnal crabs you might have seen at the beach, the Crab Bot is programmed to avoid light! If any of its sensors detect light, the Crab Bot will move away from the light source.<\/p>\n<p>This is the Crab Bot&#8217;s pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the top left, center, and right IR sensors<\/li>\n<li>If the light is shining from the left, move to the right.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if the light is shining from the right, move to the left.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if the light is shining from the center, move back and forth.<\/li>\n<li>Else, stop.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404c54\" name=\"6a22165404c54\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Set up the motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The first thing you need to do is include the Smart Inventor library at the top of your code. Next, in void setup(), include your motors.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404cae\" name=\"6a22165404cae\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Base level of the sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Each sensor corresponds to a pin on the Smart Inventor Board, and those need to be read for anything to happen with your Crab Bot! Underneath the Smart Inventor library and before void setup(), set variables for each sensors&#8217; base values. Use those variables in void setup() so the sensors will know if they&#8217;re seeing a value that isn&#8217;t normal. Add a buffer of 50 to leave some room for error.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint leftBaseLevel;\r\nint centerBaseLevel;\r\nint rightBaseLevel;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n    \r\n    leftBaseLevel = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n    centerBaseLevel = analogRead(20) - 50;\r\n    rightBaseLevel = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404cff\" name=\"6a22165404cff\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Read the sensors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In void loop(), set variables for each sensor so that they get and save the value that is being read from their corresponding pin.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\nint leftBaseLevel;\r\nint centerBaseLevel;\r\nint rightBaseLevel;\r\n \r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n\r\n    leftBaseLevel = analogRead(19) - 50;\r\n    centerBaseLevel = analogRead(20) - 50;\r\n    rightBaseLevel = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404d58\" name=\"6a22165404d58\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Left sensor<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next up: the main section of the code! You&#8217;ll need to use an if statement to check if the left sensor has detected any light. This would bring the value of the left sensor lower than the value of its base level. If the left sensor detects light, the left LEDs will light up and the Crab Bot will move to the right.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; leftBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404da8\" name=\"6a22165404da8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Right sensor<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You&#8217;re going to do the same thing for the right sensor, but you&#8217;ll need to use an else if statement instead of an if statement. This means that your code will only check it if the last if statement about the left sensor was false.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {    \r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);    \r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);    \r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);    \r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; leftBaseLevel)    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);    \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move right \r\n    }   \r\n    else if(rightSensor &lt; rightBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);\r\n\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404df7\" name=\"6a22165404df7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Center sensor<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Add another else if statement so that when the center sensor detects light, the Crab Bot will move back and forth.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {    \r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);    \r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);    \r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);    \r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; leftBaseLevel)    \r\n    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);    \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move right    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(rightSensor &lt; rightBaseLevel)    \r\n    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);        \r\n    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right    \r\n    }\r\n    else if(centerSensor &lt; centerBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);\r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n        delay(100);\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left\r\n        delay(100);\r\n\r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n        delay(100);\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left\r\n        delay(100);    \r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404e4c\" name=\"6a22165404e4c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Stop the motors<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Finally, add an else statement so the Crab Bot stops if the sensors don&#8217;t detect any light.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);\r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);\r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);\r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; leftBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n    }    \r\n\r\n    else if(rightSensor &lt; rightBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);\r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    else if(centerSensor &lt; centerBaseLevel)\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);\r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n        delay(100);\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left\r\n        delay(100);\r\n\r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right\r\n        delay(100);\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left\r\n        delay(100);\r\n    }\r\n    else\r\n    {\r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the middle LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);\r\n    \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ stop\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22165404e9d\" name=\"6a22165404e9d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint leftBaseLevel;\r\nint centerBaseLevel;\r\nint rightBaseLevel; \r\n\r\nvoid setup() {    \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();        \r\n\r\n    leftBaseLevel = analogRead(19) - 50;    \r\n    centerBaseLevel = analogRead(20) - 50;    \r\n    rightBaseLevel = analogRead(21) - 50;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {    \r\n    int leftSensor = analogRead(19);    \r\n    int centerSensor = analogRead(20);    \r\n    int rightSensor = analogRead(21);    \r\n\r\n    if(leftSensor &lt; leftBaseLevel)    \r\n    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);        \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move right    \r\n    }        \r\n    else if(rightSensor &lt; rightBaseLevel)    \r\n    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);        \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(centerSensor &lt; centerBaseLevel)    \r\n    {           \r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the right LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);           \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, HIGH);        \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right        \r\n        delay(100);        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left        \r\n        delay(100);        \r\n\r\n        digitalWrite(11, HIGH); \/\/ light the left LEDs        \r\n        digitalWrite(15, HIGH);        \r\n        digitalWrite(12, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(17, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);        \r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);        \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ move right        \r\n        delay(100);            \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ move left        \r\n        delay(100);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else    \r\n    {        \r\n        digitalWrite(11, LOW); \/\/ light the middle LEDs\r\n        digitalWrite(15, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(12, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(17, HIGH);\r\n        digitalWrite(13, LOW);\r\n        digitalWrite(18, LOW);            \r\n\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ stop    \r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Briefing videos [vc_column_text]These videos go over how to program your Crab Bot. Don't forget to go through the rest of the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Njkp6r53Vas\" align=\"center\"][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=HJqWuFykMiE\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-crab-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1742,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1811,1808,1793,1913,1915,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2218,2220,2122,2172,2171,2189],"class_list":["post-1366","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-computer-science","lesson-tag-crab","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-sensors","module-crab","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1366","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1366\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1540,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1366\/revisions\/1540"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1742"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1366"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1366"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1366"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}